WebKit: the GLib IPC connection on stream sockets on Darwin

WPE's processes talk over a Unix socket pair of type SOCK_SEQPACKET, which
Darwin's Unix sockets do not have (socketpair fails, and the UI process
stops at its first connection). Its datagram sockets keep message
boundaries, but report a full buffer as ENOBUFS while poll() calls them
writable, and give no peer credentials. A stream socket has flow control,
end of file and credentials: there each message goes as a frame, its size
and the number of file descriptors sent with it (on its first byte)
before it. The receiver keeps what came of the next frame and the file
descriptors in order; the rest of a frame the socket took only part of is
sent before any other message.

